<Layout title="Hiring Software Engineers in Poland vs Romania: B2B vs EOR Math 2026">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schemaData)} />

  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 text-slate-100">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <div class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-rose-400 uppercase mb-3">Global Employment Engineering • Eastern Europe Hiring</div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white mb-6 leading-tight">
        Hiring Software Engineers in Poland vs Romania: B2B Ryczałt vs Microenterprise EOR Math (2026)
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        An exhaustive financial modeling teardown comparing total employer cost, mandatory social security contributions, corporate tax regimes, and engineer take-home pay in Eastern Europe’s two largest developer hubs.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Google Quick Answer Callout -->
    <div class="bg-slate-900/80 border-l-4 border-rose-500 rounded-xl p-6 mb-10 shadow-lg backdrop-blur-sm">
      <div class="text-xs uppercase font-bold text-rose-400 mb-2">Google Quick Answer</div>
      <p class="text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <strong>Hiring senior software engineers via direct B2B contractor models saves US/EU tech companies 38% compared to traditional EOR employment in Poland and Romania.</strong> Poland’s <strong>12% B2B Ryczałt flat tax</strong> provides developers with ~81% net take-home pay on an $80k annual salary, while Romania’s <strong>3% micro-company (SRL) tax + 8% dividend tax</strong> yields ~84% net take-home. In contrast, using an Employer of Record (EOR) adds 20.48% in employer payroll taxes in Poland plus $6,000/year in platform SaaS fees.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. The Eastern European Tech Talent Landscape</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Poland and Romania represent the premier technical engineering powerhouses in the European Union, home to over 430,000 and 200,000 professional software developers respectively. Driven by rigorous university STEM curricula, high English proficiency (ranking in the top 15 globally on the EF EPI index), and overlapping timezones with Western Europe (CET / EET), both nations are primary hubs for remote US, UK, and German tech companies.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          However, the structural mechanisms through which tech companies engage these engineers differ dramatically between formal employment (*Umowa o Pracę* in Poland, *Contract Individual de Muncă* in Romania) and business-to-business (B2B) contractor frameworks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. Polish B2B Ryczałt (12%) vs Employment Contract (UoP)</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Over 75% of senior developers in Poland operate as sole proprietorships (*Jednoosobowa Działalność Gospodarcza* - JDG), invoicing tech employers via the lump-sum flat tax (**Ryczałt**):
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>12% Flat Income Tax:</strong> IT services and software architecture (PKWiU 62.01) are taxed at a flat 12% of gross revenue, completely bypassing the standard progressive tax brackets (12% up to 120,000 PLN, jumping to 32% thereafter).</li>
          <li><strong>Fixed ZUS Contributions:</strong> Healthcare and social security contributions (ZUS) are calculated based on enterprise revenue tiers rather than uncapped percentages, averaging ~$750–$880 USD per month.</li>
          <li><strong>Employer Cost Advantage:</strong> Engaging an engineer via B2B incurs zero employer-side payroll tax. Under an employment contract (UoP), the employer must pay an additional 20.48% in mandatory social insurance on top of gross salary.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Romanian Microenterprise (SRL) vs CIM Employment</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          In Romania, top-tier engineers establish a limited liability company (**SRL**) and register under the specialized microenterprise tax regime:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>1% or 3% Revenue Tax:</strong> If annual billings are under €60,000, the corporate tax is just 1% (provided one minimum-wage employee is on payroll). Between €60,000 and €500,000, the corporate tax rate is 3%.</li>
          <li><strong>8% Dividend Tax:</strong> Profits distributed to the founder are subject to an 8% flat dividend tax, alongside a capped annual health contribution (CASS) of approximately €1,800 to €3,600 EUR per year.</li>
          <li><strong>CIM Employment Contrast:</strong> Standard Romanian labor contracts (CIM) impose a crushing 41.5% combined employee tax/social contribution burden, making formal employment highly unpopular among senior software engineers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Full Financial Model: $80,000 Senior Engineer Total Cost & Take-Home</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The following benchmark models an enterprise engaging a Senior Full-Stack Engineer at an $80,000 USD annual compensation target across all four hiring structures:
        </p>

        <!-- Financial Model Table -->
        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse border border-slate-700 text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="bg-slate-950 text-slate-200">
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700">Cost & Tax Metric</th>
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700">Poland Direct B2B (Ryczałt 12%)</th>
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700">Poland EOR Employment</th>
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700 text-rose-400 font-bold">Romania Direct B2B (SRL 3%)</th>
                <th class="p-3 border border-slate-700">Romania EOR Employment</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 text-slate-300">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Gross Invoiced / Base Salary</td>
                <td class="p-3">$80,000</td>
                <td class="p-3">$80,000</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-300 font-semibold">$80,000</td>
                <td class="p-3">$80,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Employer Mandatory Taxes</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$0 (B2B)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">$16,384 (20.48% ZUS)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$0 (B2B)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-amber-300">$1,800 (2.25% CAM)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">EOR Platform SaaS Fees</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$0</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">$7,188 ($599/mo)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$0</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">$7,188 ($599/mo)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-950 font-bold text-white">
                <td class="p-3">Total Cost to Employer</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$80,000 / yr</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">$103,572 / yr</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$80,000 / yr</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-amber-300">$88,988 / yr</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Engineer Taxes & Social Deductions</td>
                <td class="p-3">$9,600 (Tax) + $8,800 (ZUS)</td>
                <td class="p-3">$24,800 (Employee Tax+ZUS)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-300">$2,400 (Corp) + $6,208 (Div)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">$33,200 (41.5% CIM Tax)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="bg-slate-950 font-bold text-white">
                <td class="p-3">Engineer Net Take-Home Pay</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-300 font-bold">$61,600 (77.0%)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-400">$55,200 (69.0%)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">$67,592 (84.5%)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">$46,800 (58.5%)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Managing Contractor Misclassification & PE Risks</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          While direct B2B contractor hiring provides enormous economic savings for both the company and the engineer, companies must protect against **Permanent Establishment (PE)** and disguised employment audits under local labor laws:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Autonomy in Execution:</strong> Contracts must specify deliverables rather than fixed daily working hours. Avoid mandating 9-to-5 synchronous presence.</li>
          <li><strong>Ownership of Tools:</strong> The engineer should furnish their own hardware and development environment. If the company issues a corporate MacBook, document it under an explicit hardware licensing agreement.</li>
          <li><strong>Non-Exclusive Engagements:</strong> Polish and Romanian tax authorities evaluate whether the contractor has the legal right to service other clients simultaneously.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Summary: Hiring Recommendation</h2>
        <div class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6 text-slate-300 space-y-3">
          <p class="font-semibold text-white">Strategic Hiring Verdict:</p>
          <p>1. <strong>Poland is the premier choice for senior AI & backend systems engineers:</strong> The talent pool is massive, enterprise English is fluent, and developers universally embrace the 12% Ryczałt B2B model.</p>
          <p>2. <strong>Romania delivers the highest net take-home pay:</strong> The 3% micro-company structure gives developers exceptional financial retention, enabling competitive offers at lower gross billing rates.</p>
          <p>3. <strong>Use EOR only when equity or collective bargaining mandates employment:</strong> For standard remote software engineering, direct B2B contracts with compliant IP assignment clauses save up to $23,000/year per senior hire.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
